      "    28°44'20\" at the top to 28°43'20\" at the bottom. The angular difference is: 28°44'20\" -\n",
      "    28°43'20\" = 1'0\" = 60 arcseconds = 1 arcminute. However, examining the axis more carefully,\n",
      "    the full range shown is from approximately 28°44'20\" to 28°36'20\" (reading from top to\n",
      "    bottom), which would give 8 arcminutes (480 arcseconds). The visible tick marks and labels\n",
